From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lctech f1c200s: CPU OPP table for cpufreq-dt (stock 408, overclock steps to 792 MHz)

Give cpu0 its clock (CLK_CPU) and an operating-points-v2 table so
cpufreq-dt can switch pll-cpu at runtime: 408 MHz (the chip's stock clock,
which U-Boot sets) and overclock steps at 528/600/648/720/792 MHz for
finding the chip's headroom without reflashing the bootloader. The CCU
already parks the CPU on osc24M while pll-cpu relocks. No voltage
scaling: the board's core rail is fixed at 1.2 V. The kernel config makes
the userspace governor the default, so nothing changes until a frequency
is written to scaling_setspeed.
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/suniv-f1c200s-lctech-pi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/suniv-f1c200s-lctech-pi.dts
@@ -459,3 +459,56 @@
 		status = "okay";
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * CPU frequency (cpufreq-dt; the board linux.fragment makes the userspace
+ * governor the default, so the CPU stays at the 408 MHz U-Boot sets until a
+ * frequency is written to scaling_setspeed). 408 MHz is the chip's stock
+ * clock; every step above it is an overclock, here for finding this chip's
+ * headroom: reports on the same F1C200s put most chips at ~648 MHz and some
+ * at 720 MHz at stock voltage. No voltage scaling: the board's core rail is
+ * fixed at 1.2 V (EA3036 buck, schematic "CORE 1.2V"). pll-cpu is 24 MHz * N
+ * here, so every step is exact; the CCU parks the CPU on osc24M while the PLL
+ * relocks.
+ */
+&{/cpus/cpu@0} {
+	clocks = <&ccu CLK_CPU>;
+	operating-points-v2 = <&cpu_opp_table>;
+};
+
+/ {
+	cpu_opp_table: opp-table-cpu {
+		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+		opp-shared;
+
+		opp-408000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <408000000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <244144>; /* 8 32k periods */
+		};
+
+		opp-528000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <528000000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <244144>;
+		};
+
+		opp-600000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <600000000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <244144>;
+		};
+
+		opp-648000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <648000000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <244144>;
+		};
+
+		opp-720000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <720000000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <244144>;
+		};
+
+		opp-792000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <792000000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <244144>;
+		};
+	};
+};
